From e372e44cacc1b3afa2fb6d724e5633ede21721b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:16:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 50/54] render: text wraps at maxwidth, stops at maxrows, takes
 spacing and script-set alignment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires the rest of WE's layout (GH 0x1401dd330, in TextLayout since the previous patch) to the
text's properties, each only while its switch is on (GH 0x14027c600: maxwidth with flag 4 =
limitwidth, maxrows with flag 8 = limitrows):
- limitwidth: a glyph (not the line's first, not a space) whose right edge passes maxwidth breaks
  the line at the last space before it, or at it in a longer word; the rest, less its leading
  spaces, is the next line and the line's trailing spaces go.
- limitrows: lines past maxrows are dropped. A wrap that would pass it instead ends the line: with
  limituseellipsis shortened a character at a time until it fits with "…" after it, without it cut
  at the glyph. An explicit line past maxrows ends the last kept one the same way.
- blockalign: a wrapped line's spaces share what it lacks of maxwidth (justified).
- spacing: x per glyph advance, y per line.
- maxwidth and maxrows are layer properties (a script on maxwidth sizes song titles to their box);
  ITextLayer.horizontalalign / verticalalign are writable from scripts and relayout the next frame
  (S28: 6 scenes write them).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B4 (T2, T5, S28)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8XbjUdhpEVfhFbe7bj
